WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.273
So, Tim reminds me of, does
anybody here know Patrick Lencioni?

2
00:00:06.273 --> 00:00:07.274
He's written a number of books.

3
00:00:07.274 --> 00:00:09.860
He wrote a book called The
Five Dysfunctions of a Team.

4
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.904
And in that book, he writes it.

5
00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:14.657
This is a very simple statement,
but the statement just goes like this.

6
00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:17.785
He said, It's not strategy.

7
00:00:17.785 --> 00:00:21.247
It's not information, it's not technology.

8
00:00:21.247 --> 00:00:24.959
It's none of these things that
actually give you the edge.

9
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:29.755
The single thing that gives you the edge
to actually build something is teamwork.

10
00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:33.384
And so I really want
you to think about that.

11
00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:34.843
It's not the people.

12
00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.513
People don't give you the edge.

13
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.683
We go out then, we recruit
the best, that's fine.

14
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:42.893
But it's how they work together.

15
00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:48.650
It's that part of the culture that
actually gets people to perform,

16
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:53.988
to perform significantly, if you will,
in ways that you wouldn't think it's them.

